      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T14:18:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we find a different names for this? Persistent mapping in the D3D12/Vulkan/GL sense is a different feature.\n\nInstead this is an optimization to eagerly remap buffers to allow mapAsync+WaitAny(0) to complete the mapping future without taking locks, if the application previously ensured that all previous GPU operations using the buffer completed.\n\nLet\u0027s also clarify on the linked issue that this is not \"persistent mapping\".",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "469864ef_ae085bf0",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-04T14:29:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have renamed the toggle to \"Auto Map Backend Buffer\".\n\nanw, TBH I still think the \"emulation\" part of the old name already distinguishes itself from the true \"persistent map\" in other APIs. Even if in future we want to expose true \"persistent map\" to users. The emulation here still works, users don\u0027t need to call `MapAsync`, `Unmap`, they only need to call `GetMappedRange` after GPU finishes using the buffer to get the up-to-date mapped pointer. Thus the semantic \"persistent map\" is still somewhat correct minus the mapped ptr part.",
      "parentUuid": "852b5a63_aa71c6ed",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5116dec_b58dffb2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-04T16:06:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the iteration, it looks much better now (and the end state after finching even better if it is successful).\n\nThe difficulty with \"persistent mapping\" is also that when buffers are persistently mapped, developers expect to be able to write to buffer on worker threads whenever they want, even during the execution of a queue::Submit which wouldn\u0027t be possible here. Thanks for the rename to \"auto map\", it makes the semantic more clear.",
      "parentUuid": "469864ef_ae085bf0",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e47ff4b6_5bd7be81",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T14:18:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we do it unconditionally? It should be cheap.",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53725d1e_7ec6c326",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T14:40:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I want to do A/B test to see whether it\u0027s an improvement before we remove the other path. Mapping buffers all the time is not free. What if we map buffer but users never use it. Also in future, Graphite could use a buffer repeatedly in different Queue::Submit, forcing the buffer to map, unmapped constantly for nothing. Unfortunately, D3D11 doesn\u0027t have explicit `FlushMappedRange` function, hence every `Unmap` would result in a flush AFAIK.",
      "parentUuid": "e47ff4b6_5bd7be81",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55863a3c_19f6574b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T14:54:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For writable buffers, we use `D3D11_MAP_WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE`. It\u0027s probably quite cheap if we don\u0027t write anything between map calls. However, I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s guaranteed. So a toggle allows us to revisit the old path again in future if the architecture of Graphite changes. No to mention the extra book keepings in the Queue when all bufers are eagerly mapped seems like it would add overheads if there are many buffers.",
      "parentUuid": "53725d1e_7ec6c326",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0ad5b530_16912523",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 9,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T16:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mmmmh keeping the code for A/B testing is a bit unfortunate given that it makes things much more complex. But I guess we can have that complexity temporarily for ~3 months.\n\n\u003e What if we map buffer but users never use it.\n\nThat seems fine, the main cost would be CPU cache invalidation of cache lines that we aren\u0027t going to access in this case.\n\n\u003e Also in future, Graphite could use a buffer repeatedly in different Queue::Submit, forcing the buffer to map, unmapped constantly for nothing.\n\nIf it uses it constantly, the check whether we can EagerRemap will fail all the time and no D3D11 calls will happen. It\u0027s a bit unnecessary to keep adding the buffer to a list for nothing, but that cost should be somewhat minimal I\u0027d imagine.\n\n\u003e For writable buffers, we use D3D11_MAP_WRITE_NO_OVERWRITE.\n\nMy understanding is that this flag is used to tell the driver that we promise to not overwrite a buffer that\u0027s already used on the GPU. But since we already guarantee that at the WebGPU level, maybe `D3D11_MAP_WRITE` ends up the same in the D3D11 driver?",
      "parentUuid": "53725d1e_7ec6c326",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
