    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d16ca5c_31059b58",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 615,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T14:40:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do you mean we should eager map when we first create the buffer then ignore this 1st map optimization?\n\nThat would create the shadow copy for nothing. For example, with MapRead buffers, typically the buffers are copied to using GPU then Map for read. If we always mapped it at creation, if there are contentions, a shadow copy would be created but then unused. It\u0027s a waste.\n\nSimilarly, for MapWrite buffers, it\u0027s also the same, some times, users didn\u0027t map it then used in the queue immediately, a shadow copy would be created for nothing. It\u0027s especially expensive for big buffers.",
      "parentUuid": "a5a5b947_ceff1d64",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 612,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 615,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b8081b2e_618b23ff",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 615,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T16:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually I was curious why we need to handle the first map specially here. But it sounds like it is because with eager remapping we expect buffers unused on the GPU to be available immediately for the CPU, including for the first map. But also we don\u0027t want to do that mapping on creation because it might be unnecessary if the buffer ends up being used on the GPU before the first time it is mapped.\n\nOne thing that seems to make this CL difficult is that D3D11 requires a staging buffer for MAP_READ while MAP_WRITE works with the other GPU usable buffers.\n\nThe only ways for a GPUUsableBuffer to be written on the GPU is via QueryResolve, storage-write, and copies from other buffer. (copies from textures actually do a readback right now). If the application does a copy into a MapRead buffer, it seems likely that they will want to readback, so at the end of the submit making the Stagin storage the active one seems like it would make sense.\n\nAnd it would allow support for eager remapping of MapRead|MapWrite. Do you think that\u0027s insane?",
      "parentUuid": "1d16ca5c_31059b58",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 612,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 615,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
