      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T14:40:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s needed for cancelling the scheduled remap after being destroyed.\n\nExample:\n- Queue.CopyBufferToBuffer()\n  - Buffer.UnmapIfNeeded()\n  - Queue.TrackPendingMapBuffer() --\u003e schedule a remap when this submit completes.\n- Buffer.Destroy()\n  - We need to cancel the above remap otherwise it would access released buffer pointers.\n  - We could also set last usage serial to max value instead of using `mMapReadySerial`. But it\u0027s the same concept, we need a way to cancel.",
      "parentUuid": "33f763a4_d96fe75e",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94c33dd8_59b86441",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 748,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-03T16:05:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ideally we could check `GetState` of the buffer in `MapReady`, or is there a race as well?",
      "parentUuid": "1e5d6c9d_a57b1d24",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88319c94_318606c3",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d11/BufferD3D11.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 748,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003501
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-04T14:29:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could check `IsAlive` or `GetState` in the scheduled map function. However that\u0027s because `Destroy`, `Tick` and `WaitAny` are protected by the device\u0027s lock currently. Thus checking the buffer\u0027s front-end state is safe.\n\nIn future, we might want to remove the device\u0027s lock from the `Destroy` function. At that point,`IsAlive` wouldn\u0027t be relied on here. Because the scheduled mappings are processed by `Device::Tick` or `WaitAny`\u0027s flow. Those functions won\u0027t be prevented from running concurrently with the buffer\u0027s `Destroy`. I already have several solutions for this, it will be handled in an upcoming CL.",
      "parentUuid": "94c33dd8_59b86441",
      "revId": "a335988ca841282f1e2ad9882553e5cee907d5f0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
